            <ArticleTitle>Pain therapy: from theoretical research to clinical application.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>169-74</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>After a brief review of the supraspinal and spinal effects of morphine, the reference substance for studies on analgesia, the authors expose a synthesis of the recent literature regarding neurotransmitter involvement in pain perception and transmission. From these data, some future prospects for pain treatment research are identified.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
